ContextKeeper — Product Requirements Document (PRD)
Product name: ContextKeeper
Tagline: Your files remember, so you don't have to.
Challenge: Hacktoberfest 2026 — Open-Source AI Challenge, Week 3: Slow and Steady
Primary AI model: Google Gemma (open-weight)
Development environment: Google AI Studio Build mode
Target platform: Responsive web application
Primary goal: Deliver a functional, demonstrable AI-powered personal knowledge library that reduces the effort of organizing and finding forgotten information.
________________


1. Product Overview
1.1 The problem
People continuously accumulate digital information: PDFs, screenshots, research papers, tutorials, notes, downloaded resources, project documentation, and other files.
Over time, these files become difficult to manage. Users forget filenames, lose track of where they saved documents, and struggle to remember which file contained a particular piece of information.
Traditional file organization depends heavily on manual effort. Users must rename files, create folders, assign categories, and remember their own organizational systems. Conventional filename search also fails when a user remembers the content of a document but not its name.
Existing AI document-chat tools often focus on asking questions about individual documents. ContextKeeper instead focuses on the broader problem of maintaining and retrieving useful context across a personal collection of files.
1.2 The solution
ContextKeeper is an AI-powered personal librarian that automatically understands, organizes, connects, and retrieves information from a user's digital documents.
Users upload files, allow ContextKeeper to index them, and then search their collection using natural language. The application returns relevant documents, explains why each result matches, and provides evidence from the original source.
The user should not need to manually organize every file before the library becomes useful.
1.3 Product vision
Create a personal knowledge library that becomes more useful as users add information, while requiring as little ongoing organization as possible.
1.4 Product promise
Save it once. Find it when you need it.
ContextKeeper should reduce the cognitive load associated with remembering filenames, maintaining folder structures, and repeatedly searching through large collections of digital information.
