2. Target Users
Primary users
Students and researchers
* Save lecture notes, papers, research materials, and reference documents.
* Need to recover information from previously downloaded resources.
* Often remember an idea but not the title or filename of its source.
Developers and technology professionals
* Accumulate tutorials, documentation, code notes, setup guides, and project references.
* Need to retrieve information from past projects without manually inspecting every file.
Job seekers and professionals
* Collect CV versions, application instructions, job descriptions, certificates, and career resources.
* Need to retrieve specific documents or information quickly.
Personal knowledge collectors
* Save articles, screenshots, PDFs, and miscellaneous resources for future use.
* Want a searchable personal library without the overhead of maintaining a complex knowledge-management system.
Primary user need
“I know I saved something useful, but I don't remember its filename, where it is, or exactly which document contains it.”
Secondary user need
“I have too many files to organize manually, and I want them to become searchable and useful without spending hours sorting them.”
