3. Core User Experience
The application must deliver this complete workflow:
1. The user opens ContextKeeper.
2. The user uploads one or more supported documents.
3. ContextKeeper extracts their text and creates searchable document records.
4. Gemma analyzes the extracted content and generates useful summaries, topics, and contextual information.
5. The user sees the documents appear in their library.
6. The user enters a natural-language search query.
7. ContextKeeper retrieves relevant documents using search and ranking logic.
8. The interface displays matching files, relevance explanations, and source excerpts.
9. The user opens a document, copies a useful excerpt, or saves a collection.
10. The user can return to the library later without having to rebuild it.
The experience must be functional from upload to retrieval. A visually attractive interface with simulated AI results is not an acceptable implementation.
