6. Technical Architecture
Frontend
* React.
* TypeScript.
* Vite where supported by the generated project.
* Tailwind CSS or a consistent component styling system.
* Accessible, reusable interface components.
* IndexedDB for browser-side persistence.
Backend
* Node.js server-side runtime supported by Google AI Studio.
* TypeScript.
* Secure server-side calls to the Gemma inference API.
* Document extraction and processing.
* Search and ranking orchestration.
* Runtime validation of model responses.
* Centralized error handling.
Document processing
* PDF text extraction with a suitable maintained library.
* Native text reading for TXT and Markdown.
* Validation of uploaded file types and sizes.
* Normalization of extracted text.
* Stable identifiers for documents and source excerpts.
Search
* Full-text search over extracted text and metadata.
* Semantic retrieval using a compatible embedding mechanism where feasible.
* Ranking that considers content relevance and exact matches.
* Evidence snippets linked to their source documents.
The initial release does not require a separate vector database. Do not introduce unnecessary infrastructure before the core workflow is reliable.
Persistence
* IndexedDB for the user's local library.
* No mandatory authentication.
* No mandatory cloud database.
* No cloud synchronization in the MVP.
Hosting
Use Google AI Studio's supported preview and deployment workflow initially. Keep the code exportable and suitable for eventual GitHub publication and independent deployment.
